{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + weighted fusion (config_045, 0.725 acc) is the best configuration, and transformer aggregation is the only aggregation tested with this top combination. The key uncertainty is whether the transformer aggregation layer is actually contributing meaningful performance over a simpler avgpool, or whether the strong scvi_n200 encoder makes the aggregation strategy less critical. Config_003 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) isolates this question by changing only the aggregation from transformer to avgpool while keeping all other top-performing components fixed. If avgpool performs comparably (~0.70+), it confirms a cheaper architecture is viable, saving GPU hours for the remaining 4 experiments to explore other directions. If it drops significantly, we confirm transformer is essential and can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning other aspects. Expected relative cost: moderate-to-low (~2-2.5 GPU hours), roughly 30-40% cheaper than the transformer-based config_045 (3.60 GPU hours), since avgpool eliminates the transformer self-attention layers over profiles."
}

